termcall bundles a static build of FFmpeg inside its release binaries.

FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3. It is
executed as a separate program -- termcall starts it and reads its output --
and is not linked into termcall, so the two remain separately licensed:
termcall is MIT, the bundled FFmpeg is GPLv3.

The FFmpeg licence text ships alongside each release as FFMPEG-LICENSE.txt.
FFmpeg source is available from https://ffmpeg.org/download.html, and the
particular builds bundled here come from
https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static (release b6.1.1).

Building termcall without `-tags embedffmpeg` produces a binary that carries
no FFmpeg at all and uses whatever is installed on the machine.
